<h2>Multiplication Game Day</h2>
<p><strong>Original 2021 learning goal:</strong> Practice finding products within 100 by playing multiplication games.</p>
<p>Warm-up Number Talk: 4 × 10 = 40, 4 × 20 = 80, 4 × 21 = 84, and 4 × 24 = 96. Reuse 4 × 20 and add groups of four, or use 4 × 25 = 100 and subtract 4.</p>
<h3>Rectangle Rumble</h3><p>Play in pairs with different rectangle colors and factor spinners; represent products by grid rectangles, total area and explain who wins. Teacher evaluates actual cards, drawings, images, and oral work where required.</p>
<h3>How Close? Multiply to 100</h3><p>Use four cards per partner, choose two or three values to multiply, score the absolute distance to 100 and sum round scores. Teacher evaluates actual cards, drawings, images, and oral work where required.</p>
<h3>Choice Time: Multiplication Games</h3><p>Choose Compare, How Close? or Rectangle Rumble; demonstrate a strategy in the real selected center. Teacher evaluates actual cards, drawings, images, and oral work where required.</p>
